motion.in-position must not go TRUE while a joint still moves.

Two ways it did, both at the end of a move, by a few servo cycles:

- In coord and teleop mode a joint's command is the cubic interpolator's
  output over the planner's positions, which trails the planner by a few
  cycles. In-position followed the planner, not the joints.
- In teleop, a jog stop cleared the jog's active flag at once, while its
  planner still decelerated: in-position came up mid-deceleration.

Task waits on in-position before M-codes, I/O, the end of an MDI command and
mode switches, and test helpers wait on it for "the machine has stopped".

inpos_latch (from motion/jerk-coord-inpos) records the joint command at
each rising edge of motion.in-position, in the servo thread. After an MDI G0
and after a teleop jog stop, the command at the edge must be where the joint
then rests, exactly.
